license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A Python library for learning the structure of Bayesian networks, and the
  causal structure behind them, from data held in one place: greedy
  equivalence search (GES) and XGES over BDeu, BIC or Gaussian BIC, iterated
  local search over variable orders, FLOP, hill climbing and tabu search over
  DAGs, and exact search by dynamic programming or integer programming. The
  scores and graph routines are compiled; structural metrics, XMLBIF input,
  forward sampling and five benchmark networks are included. The federated
  methods of fedcausal build on it.
keywords:
  - causal discovery
  - structure learning
  - Bayesian networks
  - greedy equivalence search
  - BDeu
  - order search
